s not apply here. This move captures three internal pieces (C6, D5, E4), flipping them to the user's color, and does not expose a new corner to the opponent.\n\nReason: Move B7 is the safest and most logical choice. G2 immediately gives the opponent the H1 corner, and B2 risks the A1 corner. B7 is played next to a corner the opponent already owns, negating the positional risk, while securing a good capture of internal discs.\n\nAnswer: (B, 7)"}
